# Solve for Disappointment against a hand of only lands and an instant: the hand is revealed and, with no nonland permanent
# card in it, no choice is made (CR 608.2d; the bare refusal fails if a question is put), so nothing is discarded. The spell
# resolved, so its last instruction still happens: empower Jace makes a Jace token with one loyalty counter (CR 701.71a).

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Solve for Disappointment
Swamp x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Lightning Bolt
Island x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Solve for Disappointment.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
! Bot1.Choose
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Solve for Disappointment
Bot1.Battlefield.Jace Token.Counters.Loyalty = 1
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Hand.Count = 7
